{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>Abraham your father.</b> This teaches that the children of children are like children." "<b>The land upon which you lie.</b> What is the novelty? Rather, by giving you a little land, from there you will break through in all directions and conquer all your surroundings — like the parable of what kings would do for important officers: they give them a little land, and they go and conquer by their might all their surroundings. Here Rashi explained: the Holy One, blessed be He, folded all the land of Israel under him. All this the Holy One, blessed be He, showed him in a dream, like the matter of the ladder."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:06:27.867255578Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}